# A copy of a creature spell cast for its sneak cost copies that alternative cost (CR 707.10), so the token it becomes had its
# sneak cost paid too (CR 702.190a). Bot1 attacks with Ornithopter on turn 3 and sneaks Turncoat Kunoichi in during the declare
# blockers step for {2}{W}{B}, returning the Ornithopter; Choreographed Sparks copies the Kunoichi spell. The token copy enters
# first and its trigger exiles Bot2's Elvish Mystic "instead" - for good, not until the token leaves (the original Kunoichi's
# trigger then has no target). Sparks' "At the beginning of the end step, sacrifice this token" sacrifices the token, and the
# Mystic stays in exile.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Turncoat Kunoichi
Ornithopter
Choreographed Sparks
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Elvish Mystic
Island x18

[Actions]
